{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nA single desired Jira update currently crosses `dispatch_one._update_one_scalar_update`, the generic `dispatch_apply_phases._call_with_retry`, Cloud ACLI subprocess retry, or Jira DC SDK/connection retry. A late timeout can therefore multiply physical calls or leave an accepted write ambiguous. Jira's update surface does not expose a Rebar-controlled idempotency key, so recovery needs a desired-state observation rather than blind replay.\n\n## Outcome\nProve the new provider-neutral coordination contract on one concrete postcondition: set an issue summary to an exact desired value. The Cloud path is `dispatch_one._update_one_scalar_update -> AcliClient.update_issue(key, summary=...)`; the DC path terminates at `_IssuesMixin.update_issue(key, summary=...)`. Both routes return typed outcomes from one immutable logical-operation budget. This story establishes ADR 0100; RP-03 S5 finalizes it after all operation families migrate.\n\n## Approach\n1. Define provider-neutral operation/outcome values carrying a stable logical operation id, atomic desired postcondition, physical-attempt count, terminal disposition, normalized failure scope, replay safety, provider delay, `retry_not_before`, plus bounded redacted diagnostics.\n2. Add one budget owner covering the initial write, recovery observation, and any safe replan: at most three physical invocations plus 15 seconds cumulative sleep. Use deterministic injected jitter over approximately 2s then 4s fallback delays. Reuse `_errors.parse_retry_after`; a provider delay is a lower bound.\n3. At `dispatch_one._update_one_scalar_update`, route summary-only desired-state updates to the new executor instead of `_call_with_retry(client.update_issue, ...)`. The per-family route flag selects either the new route or the untouched legacy route before any call; it never dual-sends. `dispatch_apply_phases.py` remains in scope so tests prove the migrated route cannot re-enter its generic retry wrapper.\n4. For Cloud, expose a one-process ACLI invocation seam: each physical invocation launches at most one child while preserving the existing timeout, process-group termination, partial-output capture, and reaping guarantees in `acli_subprocess.py`. Rebar does not add subprocess replay below the shared budget and does not claim control over undocumented retry inside the vendor ACLI binary.\n5. Decode Cloud exit code/stdout/stderr only from sanitized historical shapes. The corpus includes the captured exit-1 unauthorized output in `test_acli_auth_failure.py` plus ticket-sourced timeout/process evidence. An unknown shape returns an unclassified fail-loud outcome; it is never guessed to be retryable. REST observations reuse structured status/header decoding where available.\n6. For DC, `build_client_from_settings` constructs `jira.JIRA(..., max_retries=0)`. A fail-fast construction guard verifies the resulting session has zero SDK retries, following ADR 0087's single-owner pattern. The selected route calls `_IssuesMixin.update_issue` exactly once per physical invocation; connection/HTTP decoding reports to the shared budget rather than sleeping or replaying independently.\n7. On an ambiguous write timeout, perform one authoritative read within the same invocation budget. If summary equals the desired value, return recovered success. If the read conclusively shows remaining drift, a replay may occur only inside the remaining budget. If the read fails, is rate-limited, or cannot establish the postcondition, return non-replaying `commit_unknown` with deferred/retry metadata; never fall through to another write.\n8. Worked example: write attempt 1 times out; observation attempt 2 also times out. The result is `commit_unknown`/deferred after two invocations and zero additional write calls. If observation 2 instead returns the old summary, write attempt 3 may set the desired summary; no fourth call exists.\n9. Classify credential, TLS, permission, invalid-request, and other permanent failures without retry. Eligible network failures, 429, plus retryable 5xx use the shared schedule. If the authoritative delay cannot fit the remaining 15-second sleep budget, return `retry_not_before` without sleeping early or consuming a fictional attempt.\n10. Establish `docs/adr/0100-reconciler-operation-coordination.md` with the operation contract, retry owner, Jira idempotency limitation, observe-before-replay alternative, budget bounds, ADR 0084/0087 relationship, behavior deltas, and expand/contract rollback. For migrated routes, the 15-second cumulative budget intentionally supersedes ADR 0084's 60-second per-sleep cap; longer delays become `retry_not_before`.\n\n## Scope\n- `operation_outcome.py` and `retry_budget.py`: typed logical outcomes plus the sole budget owner.\n- `dispatch_one.py` and `dispatch_apply_phases.py`: concrete summary-route selection plus generic-wrapper bypass.\n- Jira Cloud adapter files: one-process execution, structured observation, output decoding, cleanup, plus the typed operation surface.\n- Jira DC `transport.py`, `retry.py`, `_issues.py`, and backend: `max_retries=0`, construction guard, provider decoding, plus the typed operation surface.\n- ADR 0100, deterministic outcome/budget tests, ACLI historical fixtures, process-reaping regressions, plus DC construction tests.\n\n## Testing\n- Fake-clock and injected-jitter tables assert exact invocation, sleep, deadline, provider-lower-bound, plus `retry_not_before` accounting with zero real sleep.\n- Stateful Cloud/DC fakes exercise success, disconnect, timeout, inconclusive observation, recovered success, 429/503, malformed delay, TLS/auth/permanent 4xx, plus exact wire counts.\n- Sanitized ACLI fixtures preserve real exit/stdout/stderr triples; unknown shapes prove fail-loud behavior. Process tests prove every timeout terminates and reaps the child group.\n- DC construction tests capture the `jira.JIRA` keyword and force a nonzero resulting session value to prove the guard fails closed.\n- Existing provider/output tests pin redaction, bounded diagnostics, and intentionally preserved fast-fail behavior. All required tests are local and credential-free.\n\n## Compatibility / Rollback\nOnly summary desired-state updates use the executor during this expand slice. The route flag can return the family to legacy dispatch before later cutover, with no dual-send. Rollback preserves successful remote effects; ambiguous results are re-observed. Intentional behavior changes are one shared three-invocation/15-second budget, long-delay deferral instead of early capped replay, fail-loud unknown ACLI shapes, and non-replaying inconclusive recovery.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Both concrete summary-update routes return the same provider-neutral outcome schema; deterministic tests assert every field.\n- [ ] Repeating one logical operation preserves its stable operation id across physical invocations; a unit test asserts identity stability.\n- [ ] Wire counters prove a logical postcondition never exceeds three physical invocations or 15 seconds cumulative sleep.\n- [ ] The migrated dispatch route bypasses `_call_with_retry`; a poison test fails if that wrapper is entered.\n- [ ] DC client construction passes `max_retries=0`; a fail-fast guard test rejects a nonzero resulting session value.\n- [ ] Provider delay acts as a lower bound; an over-budget delay returns `retry_not_before` without sleeping.\n- [ ] Permanent classifications perform one invocation; transient classifications follow the injected schedule.\n- [ ] A satisfied post-timeout observation returns recovered success without a second write.\n- [ ] A conclusively unsatisfied observation permits only the remaining-budget replay.\n- [ ] A failed or inconclusive observation returns non-replaying `commit_unknown`; the worked-example test records two invocations and one write.\n- [ ] Every ACLI timeout terminates and reaps its child process group; existing POSIX regression tests remain green.\n- [ ] Sanitized historical ACLI triples decode to expected outcomes; an unknown triple returns unclassified without retry.\n- [ ] ADR 0100 records the initial coordination contract; documentation index checks pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787024885506792001,"uuid":"882691a5-e3fa-490e-817b-fe26abe41c47"}